An unordered, forward-facing backlog; completed work and its rationale
live in the git history of this file, docs/plans/, docs/design/, and
NEWS.

Items are listed alphabetically by plan name; the order carries no
meaning. Every item has an implementation plan in docs/plans/<name>.md,
and the planning/implementation/review process (who plans, who
implements, who reviews, which gates run) is docs/plans/README.md.
"window: pre-release" marks items whose cheap form expires when 1.0-0
freezes the R and dbarts.h compatibility contracts: they need a
go/no-go decision before submission, not necessarily the work itself.
No item is deferred to post-release, and gate labels (decision-gated,
consumer-gated) rank priority rather than block work (VD 2026-07-17).

Standing fact (VD, 2026-07-06): single-chain n >= 1e5 workloads are
common. The large-n performance items are live, not consumer-gated.

items
  blocked-jacobi-trees: exact parallel tree updates via noise-splitting
    augmentation (per-tree pseudo-responses y_k ~ N(g_k, sigma^2/b),
    sum-constrained): b trees update independently per barrier at the
    cost of b-fold precision on structure moves. The single-chain
    parallelism candidate; an ESS-per-second experiment decides
    (protocol and the memory-wall bound:
    docs/design/within-chain-threading.md). low-ranked.
  forest-ranef-interweaving: RESEARCHED, NO-GO now (recorded door;
    docs/design/forest-ranef-interweaving.md, blind critique SOUND WITH
    CAVEATS). The weak-signal/small-K grouped-mixing bottleneck is
    forest-ranef confounding (several-fold and estimator-unstable, not the
    slice-era 25x; the permanent gate is benchmarks/R/grouped-mixing.R).
    No cheap ASIS exists - the forest exposes no per-group knob; the only
    real fix is a coupled-leaf collapse (marginalize b via per-group
    Woodbury), which RIDES the existing ParamScoringLeafModel seam but
    couples the constant-leaf suffstat across groups/trees on the hot path
    (~800-1300 lines, draw-changing, grouped re-record) - not worth a
    narrow-corner win with a trivial longer/parallel-chain workaround.
    Reopen with VD sign-off for a concrete weak-signal/few-groups
    application needing calibrated tau intervals. Secondary: ASIS on
    (tau, b) is cheap (builds on the landed exact-IG) but funnel-only and
    can WORSEN small-K - conditional-go only behind a full-engine prototype.
    decision-gated.
  gp-followups: sampled lengthscales (theta prior, per-sample channels,
    real cost - not the mechanical follow-up the proposal suggested);
    low-rank kernels. decision/consumer-gated.
  gpu-bart: backend-seam design waits on frontier items 4-5
    (informed-kernel + CG-leaf prototypes); memo and falsifiers in
    docs/design/gpu-bart.md and parallel-bart-frontier.md.
  group-by-exposure: public group.by beyond rbart_vi
    (grouped-random-effects.md; naming reserved). decision-gated.
  grouped-equivalence: equivalence scenario for grouped rbart_vi fits,
    only if a grouped refactor is planned.
  grow-from-root: frontier 3.1's exact informed-proposal use of the
    shared scan.
  interaction-constraints: structured sparsity and interaction limits
    on the SplitSelector seam. consumer-gated.
  negbin-real-dispersion: the recorded door out of the negative-binomial
    landing (docs/plans/negative-binomial.md; design section 2 carries
    fork B's full spec): real-valued dispersion needs a non-integer-shape
    Polya-Gamma draw, for which no exact sampler exists - shipping it
    means dbarts' first documented-approximate family (truncated
    gamma-sum, bias bounded ~1e-3 at K = 200) behind an explicit opt-in.
    The same decision gates weighted-binary's fractional weights. The
    engine seams (shape-parameterized PG helper, r-update strategy) are
    already in place; VD decides if user demand appears. Poisson family
    and grouped NB are companion doors in the design's section 7.
  python-bindings: post kernel-cleanups the engine is R-free below the
    bridge; a pybind11 facade wrapper becomes prototype-scale. horizon,
    likely out-of-repo. decision-gated. The 2026-07-17 data review
    adds: host-side ingestion validation (CSC structure, categorical
    bounds, sparse metadata assembly) lives in the R bridge and would
    need reimplementing - move it into an R-free bartcore ingest
    helper when this item opens; mixed/CSC stores also hold lifetime
    borrows anchored by R protection, an undocumented contract for
    any other host.
  repo-modernization: standing hygiene bundle. Sanitizers PR-gated
    2026-07-17 (nine consecutive green push runs met the stability
    condition). Coverage resolved (VD 2026-07-17): one-shot covr audit
    at pre-release (see the release section), no CI workflow or badge.
    Remaining: optional roxygen2 and NEWS.md migrations (do not start
    unasked);
    dbarts.h's x_test/offset_test -> xTest/offsetTest cosmetic rename,
    deferred because DBARTS_API_STRINGIZE stringizes each parameter's
    full declaration, name included, so the rename alone moves
    DBARTS_C_API_HASH and forces a MINOR bump with the stan4bart floor
    in lockstep - ride it on the next hash-moving dbarts.h change
    instead.
  sparse-extensions: in-place nonzero mutation, streaming range kernel,
    mutation on dense-backed mixed columns (sparse-columns.md landing
    notes). consumer-gated.
  survival-followups: the doors out of the survival family pair (AFT +
    discrete-time hazard both landed; records in
    docs/plans/survival-models.md, design docs/design/survival.md
    section 6): cloglog link (needs a cloglog binary family first),
    competing risks (crisk.bart's territory), left truncation, grouped
    frailty (composes with rbart_vi grouping when wanted), time-varying
    covariates in the auto-expander (available today via the manual
    person-period fit), continuous-time models. Each independent;
    demand-driven. low-ranked.
  warm-starts: the cross-grid remap over mapOldCutPointsOntoNew;
    reopen when a consumer needs new-data warm starts.
  weighted-binary: post 1.0 - integer-weight probit via replicated
    latents; arbitrary real weights need a real-shape PG sampler (IPW
    is a pseudo-likelihood trap).
  x86-simd: the commented-out linalg intrinsics bodies are NOT needed
    for compute width - the manual unroll plus the per-file -m flag
    already emits 256-bit at -O2 (measured on the bench box,
    docs/plans/simd-flag-multiversioning.md); the sole unrealized win
    is non-temporal stores at DRAM-bound n (setVectorToConstant 1.6x,
    addv 1.24x at n=1e7; they lose cache-resident, so a restore needs
    a size threshold). NT-store call RESOLVED DELETE 2026-07-17 at the
    review-perf-followups close (C6 landing note there): the fits
    compaction removed every per-sweep store-bound elementwise caller
    on the constant-leaf path, the survivors are RMW or cold, so the
    ops NT stores accelerate are no longer hot; the commented bodies
    are deleted (git history keeps them).
    Independent remainder RESOLVED 2026-07-20: SSR SIMD leaf is a MEASURED
    NO-GO (kernel <=1.6x only L1-resident, bandwidth-bound at scale; SSR is
    ~0.1% of a sweep so end-to-end <=0.05%, unmeasurable, vs a re-record + a
    permanent cross-ISA fixed-lane/no-FMA obligation; docs/design/memory-wall-
    frontier.md sec 5). Windows-arm64 NEON config LANDED dcee743 (inspection-
    only; close on a windows-11-arm runner). The live perf frontier past SIMD
    (the MEMORY WALL) is the three-lens ideation in docs/design/memory-wall-
    frontier.md - flagship the histogram-fused suffstat; first action is to
    re-profile HEAD on dbarts-bench + the Z-order run-count census. The setIndexedVectorToConstant
    dispatch-completeness sub-item is RETIRED 2026-07-17: the fits
    compaction removed its hot caller (the ~18.5% scatter share the
    stan4bart profile measured); the sole survivor is the
    function-leaf cold-start, not worth a dispatch slot.

